# motoquencer2: narrowing the gate-probability lane is NON-DESTRUCTIVE. A step
# holding a value the new mode cannot reach keeps it and keeps playing it; its
# fader just shows the nearest reachable notch, and the value only changes when
# that fader is actually moved.
#
# Two steps. Step 0 is dialled to "every odd turn" (stored 4) in trig mode; step 1
# keeps the default "always" (7, which every mode offers). The clock rises on every
# odd tick, so the steps alternate: step 0 on the 1st, 3rd, 5th, ... rising edge,
# and each pass over step 0 is one turn (turn counts from 1).
#   edge 1 (t3)  step 0, turn 1 -> odd  -> plays
#   edge 2 (t5)  step 1          -> always
#   edge 3 (t7)  step 0, turn 2 -> even -> silent
#   edge 5 (t11) step 0, turn 3 -> odd  -> plays
#   edge 7 (t15) step 0, turn 4 -> even -> silent
# At t10 the lane narrows to the random chances (0, 1, 3, 6, 7), which does NOT
# contain 4. Step 0 must go on playing on odd turns, and its fader must show the
# nearest offered notch: |3-4| = 1 beats |6-4| = 2, so stored 3 = dent 2 of 5 = 0.5.
experimental
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer2]
    numfaders       = 4
    numsteps        = 2
    fadermode       = 2
    probabilitymode = I3
    clock           = I1
    gate            = O2
>>>
@0 set I3 2
# tick1: dent 1 of the four trig notches = "every odd turn" (stored 4).
@1 move F1 0.4
@1 expect F1 0.333333 tol 1e-4
@3 set I1 1
@3 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@4 set I1 0
@5 set I1 1
@5 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@6 set I1 0
@7 set I1 1
@7 expect O2 0 tol 1e-4
@8 set I1 0
@9 set I1 1
@9 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
# tick10 (a clock low): narrow the lane to the random chances. The motor moves to
# the nearest offered dent, but the STORED value is untouched.
@10 set I1 0
@10 set I3 1
@10 expect F1 0.5 tol 1e-4
@11 set I1 1
@11 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
# tick12: reading that commanded position back must not rewrite the step to the
# dent it is merely shown at — the fader has not moved.
@12 set I1 0
@12 expect F1 0.5 tol 1e-4
@13 set I1 1
@13 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@14 set I1 0
@15 set I1 1
@15 expect O2 0 tol 1e-4
# tick16: back to the trig lane — the value is still 4, so the fader returns to
# its own dent, no harm done.
@16 set I1 0
@16 set I3 2
@16 expect F1 0.333333 tol 1e-4
@17 set I1 1
@17 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
# tick18: NOW move the fader (to the top dent, "always"). That is a real edit, so
# the value finally changes: step 0 plays on every turn from here.
@18 set I1 0
@18 move F1 1.0
@18 expect F1 1.0 tol 1e-4
@19 set I1 1
@19 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@20 set I1 0
@21 set I1 1
@21 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@22 set I1 0
# turn 6 — an even turn, silent before the edit, playing now.
@23 set I1 1
@23 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
